From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:23:44 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] XEX sections: bound names and extents by their fields and
 the image

IMAGE_SECTION_HEADER.Name is 8 bytes and has no terminating NUL when the
name is 8 characters long (Forza Motorsport 4's .XBMOVIE). Mapping it as a
C string read past the field into VirtualSize, so the section was named
".XBMOVIE\f". Bound the name by the field size.

A section's VirtualSize can also extend past the loaded image (FM4's
discardable .reloc ends 0x2ED94 bytes after it). Map only the part inside
the image; a code section that does not fit rejects the image (an empty
result), since truncating code would drop it.
---
 XenonUtils/xex.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/XenonUtils/xex.cpp b/XenonUtils/xex.cpp
index 21ee0ef..a986eac 100644
--- a/XenonUtils/xex.cpp
+++ b/XenonUtils/xex.cpp
@@ -299,8 +299,22 @@ Image Xex2LoadImage(const uint8_t* data, size_t dataSize)
             flags |= SectionFlags_Code;
         }
 
-        image.Map(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(section.Name), section.VirtualAddress, 
-            section.Misc.VirtualSize, flags, image.data.get() + section.VirtualAddress);
+        // A section name fills all 8 bytes of Name when it is 8 characters long, with no
+        // terminating NUL: never read past the field.
+        const auto* name = reinterpret_cast<const char*>(section.Name);
+
+        // A section may extend past the loaded image (Forza Motorsport 4's discardable .reloc):
+        // map only the part that exists. Code is never truncated: such an image is rejected.
+        const size_t rva = section.VirtualAddress;
+        size_t size = section.Misc.VirtualSize;
+        if (rva > image.size || size > image.size - rva)
+        {
+            if (flags & SectionFlags_Code)
+                return {};
+            size = rva < image.size ? image.size - rva : 0;
+        }
+        image.Map(std::string_view(name, strnlen(name, sizeof(section.Name))), rva, uint32_t(size), flags,
+            rva < image.size ? image.data.get() + rva : nullptr);
     }
 
     auto* imports = reinterpret_cast<const Xex2ImportHeader*>(getOptHeaderPtr(data, XEX_HEADER_IMPORT_LIBRARIES));
